  "id": "maternal-aggression",
  "term": "maternal aggression",
  "definition": "Maternal aggression is aggressive behavior shown by a mother during lactation and treated as part of the maternal behavioral profile. In the source, it is described as a maternal behavior that can be reduced when central corticotropin-releasing factor activity is increased.",
